There's a riding spoiler for vanilla (and probably applies to [S]), but 
it's more about what your chances are to saddle and mount a steed. I 
don't know of any others.

All of this info is for vanilla. I've heard nothing about any 
differences in [S]. You probably have a better choice of steed.

There are a lot of benefits to steeds, and some downsides. You get the 
speed of your steed, so if you get a very fast steed (unicorns, 
warhorses have twice base speed, ki-rin and jabberwocks can be very 
fast). You can kick a steed to make it gallop (temporary speed boost) 
but it loses some tameness. For carnivores, tameness isn't a problem 
because they eat everything.

You can fly if your steed can. I don't think you can jump a horse, never 
tried though. Once you get to basic in riding, you don't need to 
dismount to pick up items. Basic comes after moving 2000 spaces while 
riding, which is not so bad.

Steeds will take some damage for you as the enemy attacks them instead 
of you. They will do some damage (but only if attacked first, 
unfortunately).

You can't wear conflict while riding. You can't levitate your steed. 
I've never tried water walking. You can teleport and levelport with the 
steed. Saddles can be hard to come by if you don't start with one. You 
can't eat corpses off the ground while riding, but you can still pick 
them up and eat them if you're at least Basic (possible bug?).


My favorite steed is a Jabberwock. They're fast, powerful, carnivorous, 
and not too rare. Warhorses are faster and easier to get in the 
beginning though, and if it goes feral it's easy to retame.

